  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Which of the following sets is a subset of $A={4n+1\u2223n\\in {0,1,2,3}}?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we must find the elements of the set $A.$ Substituting the values $n\\in {0,1,2,3}$ into the formula $4n+1,$ we get the following elements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n=0 & \\,\u21d2\\,4(0)+1=1 \\\\ n=1 & \\,\u21d2\\,4(1)+1=5 \\\\ n=2 & \\,\u21d2\\,4(2)+1=9 \\\\ n=3 & \\,\u21d2\\,4(3)+1=13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nA={1,5,9,13}.\n$$\n\nNow, a subset of $A$ is a set whose elements are also elements of the set $A.$\n\nIn our case, $B={1,5,13}$ is a subset of $A.$\n\nIn the rest of the options, the set $B$ has elements that are not in $A,$ meaning that it is not a subset of $A.$",
